    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T22:05:08Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/2033-rest-previous-ops · PR #2822 · pinned by each_reading_guard_is_pinned_and_its_removal_fails_the_pin, the_rest_region_holds_every_column_the_simulated_earlier_operations_left, the_rest_path_cuts_what_was_left_and_keeps_the_walls, the_two_rest_modes_never_use_each_others_planner, the_rest_pass_cuts_what_the_simulated_roughing_pass_left, a_roughing_pass_that_stops_above_the_floor_leaves_the_whole_pocket, a_stock_that_cannot_be_established_is_refused_by_name, a_tilted_plane_is_refused_by_name_at_the_edit_and_at_generation, an_earlier_change_makes_the_rest_pass_stale · merges at the next cut\n\nNotes for the reviewer:\n\n- The PR is a `feat`: it adds a mode. The entered-tool mode does not change.\n- The MCP skill text (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`) does not describe the new `rest.source` key. The worker session could not write that file. That edit is owed.\n- The limits are in `docs/decisions/2033-rest-previous-ops.md`: one rest area for all levels, a band of about 1.5 cells along each wall, and Adaptive stays refused.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
